            <ArticleTitle>A simple approach for the reduction of knotted coronary catheter in the radial artery during the transradial approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E126-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Development of a catheter knot is uncommon but still a matter of concern for a catheterizing cardiologist. There are only a few case reports of percutaneous catheter unknotting in the literature. We describe for the first time a case of catheter unknotting in a radial artery using a simple technique via the transradial approach. We concluded that percutaneous catheter unknotting in a radial artery using basic and simple hardware is a good alternative option to surgical management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
